==Enemy==
Nimoy Bore's base health and damage, attack rate and speed are all inferior to Bore and most of his other variants, so in the end he may actually be the easier of the bunch. Even his 50% chance to knockback cats doesn't always work out in his favor, as it can cause cats with long backswings to attack over and over again. Nevertheless, don't take him lightly when you encounter him in [[Floating Continent (Into the Future)|Floating Continent]], especially in Chapter 3.

==Strategy==
There are two things that are important to have when facing Nimoy Bore: crowd-control and [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]]. Stall him with units such as [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] and [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Onmyoji Cat]] to reduce his pushing power while stacking attackers such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] to whittle away his health. Once frozen or slowed, [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]] or [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cat]] can be used to deliver huge damage to him. Because he gets outranged by most meatshields, the meatshields will stand out of his range, effectively giving him single target.

